    "description": "Connect an MCP server with one terminal command: claude mcp add --transport http, a name you pick and the URL. claude mcp list shows the status, and /mcp signs you in when a server needs it. Example from the Claude Code docs: the Claude Code docs server.",
    "companion_text": "Follow Promptwerk for more Claude workflows, step by step. Based on the MCP quickstart and the MCP page of the Claude Code docs; the terminal scenes are an animated view, not a screen recording. Notes from the docs: run the command in your terminal, not inside a Claude session. If Claude Code asks for permission the first time Claude calls the server, approve it. Without --scope the server is active only for you in this project; with --scope user in all your projects. Verify you trust a server before connecting it; servers that fetch external content can expose you to prompt injection. Each connected server takes some space in the context window.",
